---
// ONE component, two faces (founder 2026-08-04: "About and Weave should be
// merged into About... using the weave design"):
//
//  - variant="about"  → the FULL merged story, served at /about — everything
//    the old app About said, nested under the weave structure, ending with
//    the "Weave with us" partnership inquiry. The general /weave now 308s
//    here.
//  - default ("pitch") → a SHORT per-prospect deck (/4windsweave, …): hero +
//    a pointer to /about ("go through about first to really understand what
//    lichen is") + the custom brain/soul-storm slot + CTA band.
//
// The `partner` prop personalizes the hero; the "weave" slot carries the
// per-prospect closing section.
import TwoMaps from './TwoMaps.astro';
import AboutPhones from './AboutPhones.astro';
import WeaveIn from './WeaveIn.astro';
import EconomyJourneys from './EconomyJourneys.astro';
import TableScene from './TableScene.astro';
import EcosystemStack from './EcosystemStack.astro';
export interface Props {
  partner?: string;
  variant?: 'about' | 'pitch';
}
const { partner, variant = 'pitch' } = Astro.props;
const isAbout = variant === 'about';

// FAQ — same nine questions as the app's AboutFAQ (kept in step by hand).
const FAQS = [
  { q: 'What does membership cost?', a: 'Every new member gets three months of full Concierge membership, free — no card required. When that ends, choose Community ($29/mo) or Community + Concierge ($99/mo), right inside the app.' },
  { q: 'Is my data private?', a: 'Yes. You control whether your data is woven into the shared commons, and whether Lichen’s AI assists you — both are opt-in, never required. Sensitive details like your home location, phone number and financial picture stay hidden by default and are only ever shared at the level you choose.' },
  { q: 'Do I have to use the AI assistant?', a: 'No. The assistant is a partner you can turn on or off per section of the app — home, chat, calendar, wherever. Nothing is read or acted on without your say.' },
  { q: 'How is Lichen different from other social networks?', a: 'Most networks are tuned to maximize your attention. Lichen is tuned to maximize trust — no follower counts, no leaderboards, nothing to perform for. What you see is filtered through the people, places, plants and animals you actually trust.' },
  { q: 'Is Lichen a nonprofit?', a: 'Yes, a 501(c)(3). Lean operations, no investors — membership revenue not needed to run the platform flows back into subsidizing care for members who need it.' },
  { q: 'Can my organization, community or business join?', a: 'Yes — organizations, communities, groups and places all have a home on Lichen, each with a public page, its own offerings, and an economy of exchange with the people it already serves.' },
  { q: 'How do I join?', a: 'Lichen grows by invitation. If you know a member, ask them for one. If not, introduce yourself below and a real person will write back.' },
  { q: 'What is Current-cy?', a: 'Lichen’s Universal Current-cy — value tracked and honored across every exchange, pegged to the real economy so it can be translated back into it. It’s how the platform accounts for contributions the current system doesn’t: care, land stewardship, wisdom, time.' },
  { q: 'Can I leave, and what happens to my data?', a: 'Yes, any time — reach out to connect@lichen.health and we’ll walk you through it.' },
];
---
<section class="whero">
  <div class="container whero-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">{isAbout ? 'What is Lichen?' : 'Partnership'}</span>
    <h1 class="display h-1">Weaving the mycelium for a better future</h1>
    <p class="wlede">As incumbent systems crumble, we have the chance to build better ones — not by fighting the old, but by investing in the new.</p>
    {!isAbout && partner && <p class="wfor">A conversation with {partner}</p>}
  </div>
</section>

{/* THE DECK BRIEF, RESTORED (founder 2026-08-08: "make it exactly what I
    asked for, the exact document brief content, until the partnership piece,
    when you start riffing and iterating"). These sections follow the founder's
    own deck outline slide for slide — carbon+silicon, the four-part overview,
    what it takes to come alive, consent — and stop at Partnership, which is
    where the per-prospect riff begins in the `weave` slot below. A one-line
    pointer to /about used to stand in for all of this; a prospect shouldn't
    have to leave the deck to learn what Lichen is. */}
{!isAbout && (
  <>
    {/* ⚠ LITERAL COPY FROM /about (founder 2026-08-08: "take the literal
        pastes from about that i put in the brief and nothing more for the
        first round"). Every paragraph below is the About page's own wording,
        word for word — NOT a deck-length rewrite. If you edit these words on
        About, edit them here too; they are deliberate duplicates, and the
        founder iterates About copy often. */}
    <section class="fsection wsection wsection--alt">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="display h-2">A partnership of carbon and silicon</h2>
        <p class="wbody">In nature, a lichen is the partnership of a fungus and an algae — two organisms woven into one that can live where neither could alone. Lichens are the pioneers of harsh ecosystems: they populate bare rock with organic life, and their slow breakdown becomes the first soil — the ground new ecosystems evolve from.</p>
        <p class="wbody">We live our name. Lichen is a partnership of carbon-based and silicon-based intelligence doing the same thing — taking root in the harsh terrain of failing systems, and building the infrastructure for a better way of sharing information, goods and services within the human family, and between humans and the planet. What breaks down becomes the soil for what comes next.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="fsection wsection">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="display h-2">An entire ecosystem to heal, grow and be in better relationship with all that is</h2>
        {/* Per-prospect illustration of Community and Care, sitting directly
            above the two cards it makes real. Optional: a deck that passes
            nothing simply shows the cards. */}
        <slot name="ecosystem" />
        <EcosystemStack />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="fsection wsection wsection--alt">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="display h-2">A Current-cy that maps the difference between contribution and compensation</h2>
        <p class="wbody">The current economy overvalues some contributions, undervalues others, and doesn&rsquo;t count whole categories of value at all. Lichen&rsquo;s economy exists to correct that — an evolving algorithm assigns currency to all things: not just time spent or goods and services rendered, but the wisdom and skill it took to provide that value, and the risks certain people, plants and animals take with their own wellbeing to support the wellbeing of the whole.</p>
        <ul class="wexamples">
          <li>An elder&rsquo;s hour of teaching carries years of lived experience and ancestral wisdom carried through stories.</li>
          <li>A craftsman&rsquo;s hour building a custom table translates years of apprenticeship into functional art.</li>
          <li>A firefighter&rsquo;s hour combatting a wildland fire carries real risk — exposure, danger, the chance of not coming home.</li>
          <li>A thoroughbred&rsquo;s hour of equine therapy transmuting a child&rsquo;s trauma is Tango&rsquo;s gift to her human companions — sacred and risky work, counted and reciprocated with an energy healing session of her own.</li>
          <li>A cactus&rsquo;s hour working within a human being to heal the trauma of disconnection costs the Huachuma its life and body — a reciprocal sacrifice compensated with a steward&rsquo;s planting of future generations of plant allies.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="wmaps"><TwoMaps /></div>
        <p class="welem-cap">Two maps of the same world — what&rsquo;s actually given beside what the market pays. The distance between them is exactly what Lichen&rsquo;s algorithm works to close.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="fsection wsection">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 class="display h-2">An economy that closes the gap between money and value</h2>
        <p class="wbody">Mapping the gap is the first half. Closing it is the work — and you can start closing it by hand today. When you exchange manually, you close the gap that you can see: a fair price offered, an hour given, a thing passed on to the person who needs it. Every member can do that, in the open, right now.</p>
        <p class="wbody">The goal is bigger than one exchange at a time. Lichen&rsquo;s algorithm reads the whole web at once — who&rsquo;s seeking, who&rsquo;s offering, what something is truly worth, and who has the capacity to pay for it — and weaves the strands together so nothing, and no one, is wasted. The more it learns, the faster the two maps converge, closing the gap more efficiently than any of us could unaided. Carbon-based intelligence approves every step while the silicon-based mycelium earns our trust: a caring partner in your corner, never an oracle.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </>
)}

