  <section class="fsection wsection wsection--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="display h-2">An entire ecosystem to heal, grow and be in better relationship with all that is</h2>
      <EcosystemStack />
      <h3 class="display h-2 wsub">The corrective social network</h3>
      <p class="wbody">Most technology platforms feed you to an algorithm tuned to maximize attention, harvest fear, and drive consumption that temporarily comforts the dis-ease of disconnection because our current political and economic systems rely on human suffering to survive. Lichen holds the whole of you instead — your care and healing, your work and the things you offer, the events you gather for, the places you love, the jobs that give you purpose and fund your livelihood, and a fairer economy that values all things, not just human contributions — woven into a single web of people, plants, animals, elements, spaces, communities, groups and organizations you trust. Everything in one place, because your best life isn&rsquo;t lived in silos — or on a technology platform.</p>
      <p class="wcallout">The commons is yours to shape. Every member controls whether their data is woven into the shared web, and whether they want Lichen&rsquo;s AI as a partner in realizing their purpose — never a requirement, always a choice.</p>
      <TableScene />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fsection wsection">
    <div class="container">
      <h3 class="display h-2 wsub">Designed for reciprocity, not extraction</h3>
      <p class="wbody">If AI worries you, that&rsquo;s fair — pointed at extraction, it accelerates extraction. Pointed at reciprocity, it provides the operational brilliance to identify gaps and eliminate inefficiencies in ways that carbon-based intelligence isn&rsquo;t well suited to resolve. And that benefit is more than a business advantage — it&rsquo;s the seed of a cultural shift. When this much can be done with this little, we no longer have to force people into systems that don&rsquo;t serve them just to subsist. We can grant one another the inherent resources of survival — and free every kind of intelligence, carbon and silicon alike, for the contributions only they can make. Lichen is a place to practice that future now.</p>
      <h3 class="display h-2 wsub">You decide what&rsquo;s shared, and with whom</h3>
      <p class="wbody">Whether AI will help or hurt our capacity to build a better future isn&rsquo;t about the technology — it&rsquo;s about the consciousness of those co-creating with it. Until you feel safe partnering with silicon-based intelligence, Lichen gives you full control over whether your data is part of the collective, and whether you want Lichen&rsquo;s AI as a partner at all.</p>
      <a href="/privacy-and-ai" class="wlink">Go deeper on data, privacy and AI →</a>
      <AboutPhones />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fsection wsection">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="display h-2">Authentic connection, safety and trust you can&rsquo;t game</h2>
      <p class="wbody">What reaches you comes through your My-celium — the people, places, plants and animals you trust. Trusting people, and recommending the groups, communities, organizations and places you stand behind, are authentic person-to-person signals — never public scores. Trust stays private. A recommendation carries your name, but only to the people who already trust you. Either way there are no follower counts, no leaderboards, nothing to perform for. If something reaches you, someone you trust stands behind it.</p>
      <p class="wbody">That same web is the safety layer of the economy. Star ratings can be farmed; a path through your own relationships can&rsquo;t be faked. Browse the whole marketplace, or narrow it to people, places, groups, communities or organizations you trust — or people <em>they</em> trust — and every listing shows you your path to the person behind it: <em>&ldquo;Trusted by someone you trust&rdquo;</em> — the mutual friend you&rsquo;d want before meeting a stranger, built into the ground you walk on.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fsection wsection">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="display h-2">A Current-cy that maps the difference between contribution and compensation</h2>
      <p class="wbody">The current economy overvalues some contributions, undervalues others, and doesn&rsquo;t count whole categories of value at all. Lichen&rsquo;s economy exists to correct that — an evolving algorithm assigns currency to all things: not just time spent or goods and services rendered, but the wisdom and skill it took to provide that value, and the risks certain people, plants and animals take with their own wellbeing to support the wellbeing of the whole.</p>
