        <li>An elder&rsquo;s hour of teaching carries years of lived experience and ancestral wisdom carried through stories.</li>
        <li>A craftsman&rsquo;s hour building a custom table translates years of apprenticeship into functional art.</li>
        <li>A firefighter&rsquo;s hour combatting a wildland fire carries real risk — exposure, danger, the chance of not coming home.</li>
        <li>A thoroughbred&rsquo;s hour of equine therapy transmuting a child&rsquo;s trauma is Tango&rsquo;s gift to her human companions — sacred and risky work, counted and reciprocated with an energy healing session of her own.</li>
        <li>A cactus&rsquo;s hour working within a human being to heal the trauma of disconnection costs the Huachuma its life and body — a reciprocal sacrifice compensated with a steward&rsquo;s planting of future generations of plant allies.</li>
