      <div class="wmaps"><TwoMaps /></div>
      <p class="welem-cap">Two maps of the same world — what&rsquo;s actually given beside what the market pays. The distance between them is exactly what Lichen&rsquo;s algorithm works to close.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MAPPING THE GAP AND CLOSING IT ARE TWO DIFFERENT CLAIMS (founder
       2026-08-08). The Current-cy measures — that's the section above. This
       one is the economy that acts on the measurement: manual exchange as
       where every member starts, the algorithm as where it's going. -->
  <section class="fsection wsection">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="display h-2">An economy that closes the gap between money and value</h2>
      <p class="wbody">Mapping the gap is the first half. Closing it is the work — and you can start closing it by hand today. When you exchange manually, you close the gap that you can see: a fair price offered, an hour given, a thing passed on to the person who needs it. Every member can do that, in the open, right now.</p>
      <p class="wbody">The goal is bigger than one exchange at a time. Lichen&rsquo;s algorithm reads the whole web at once — who&rsquo;s seeking, who&rsquo;s offering, what something is truly worth, and who has the capacity to pay for it — and weaves the strands together so nothing, and no one, is wasted. The more it learns, the faster the two maps converge, closing the gap more efficiently than any of us could unaided. Carbon-based intelligence approves every step while the silicon-based mycelium earns our trust: a caring partner in your corner, never an oracle.</p>
      <h3 class="display h-2 wsub">Why philanthropy is still needed</h3>
      <p class="wbody">The systems we inherited didn&rsquo;t just deny our interconnection — they actively worked to destroy it, rewarding extraction, encouraging division, and profiting from perpetual suffering. The wounds are real. The people trapped inside them are real. And the gap between the world we have and the world we want cannot be bridged by innovation, alone.</p>
      <p class="wbody">Trauma research shows that formative experiences encode subconscious beliefs that, if not intercepted with deep and targeted healing, shape our biology and behavior for life. Being born into trauma-based systems doesn&rsquo;t just hurt — it programs. Unlearning those programs takes time, intention, and the right conditions. That is precisely why philanthropy is still needed: not as charity, but as the holding structure that creates space for genuine biological, psychological, and spiritual transformation necessary to be a contributing member in a better world.</p>
      <p class="wbody">Philanthropy is the temporary scaffolding that holds people while the new floor is built beneath them. Lichen is a nonprofit with the vision, strategy and operations of a lean technology startup — membership and donations keep the platform running, and <strong>everything beyond that flows back into the network to restore balance</strong>. Our algorithm identifies those the current system leaves behind: the people, plants, animals and places who are</p>
      <ol class="wpaths">
        <li><strong>Harmed by toxic systems</strong> — healing funded until they&rsquo;re ready to reclaim their soul&rsquo;s joy and purpose</li>
        <li><strong>Chronically undervalued by the current economy</strong> — goods and resources subsidized to close the value gap</li>
        <li><strong>Deliberately under-resourced</strong> — innovators whose ideas challenge the systems that limit us, invested in</li>
        <li><strong>Young people still becoming</strong> — the children reached before they lose their joy, curiosity and knowing</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="wbody">This is corrective investment — targeted, efficient, and designed to become obsolete. Lichen <em>pays only the gap</em>: what insurance doesn&rsquo;t cover, what organizations can&rsquo;t absorb, what individuals can&rsquo;t yet afford, what the current market won&rsquo;t fund. No further — and only until the community&rsquo;s own economy can hold everyone. Money dedicated to the commons here can never turn back into private profit — you&rsquo;re not the product; you&rsquo;re a contributing member to a better way of being in relationship with each other and the planet.</p>
      <p class="wbody">To bridge away from the systems that no longer serve the people, Lichen holds two economies, run side by side. <strong>Current-cy</strong> moves value out in the open — a transparent, dollar-pegged ledger, no speculation, the whole story visible and transferable into the incumbent economy we are all still beholden to. <strong>Offerings</strong> broker value exchanged within the ecosystem, freely, without money. One bridges the world as it is; the other builds the world as it could be.</p>
      <EconomyJourneys />
      <p class="wbody">Lichen honors non-human people. The beings we&rsquo;re in relationship with are members too — a therapy horse, a sacred plant medicine, a river — stewarded by humans, their contributions valued and reciprocated within Lichen&rsquo;s economy. Underneath every exchange runs Lichen&rsquo;s Universal Current-cy — value tracked, honored, and translated back into the wider economy.</p>
      <a href="/economy" class="wlink">Learn more about the economy →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fsection wsection wsection--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="display h-2">It takes real people, choosing to build the new</h2>
      <p class="wbody">Lichen&rsquo;s business model and technology platform are architected to serve a better society — but it only comes alive when a critical mass of humanity chooses to withdraw its energy from a failing system to enliven a better one. That looks like three things:</p>
      <ol class="wpaths">
        <li><strong>Investing in a better future</strong> — subscription revenue funds the business and technology infrastructure a better society runs on, and everything beyond our lean operating costs pours back into the network&rsquo;s rebalancing work.</li>
        <li><strong>Scaling a whole-earth renaissance</strong> — donations and seed gifts speed the platform&rsquo;s buildout and reach, growing the mycelium&rsquo;s capacity to restore balance, health and harmony.</li>
        <li><strong>Bringing a better world to life</strong> — move your calendar, events, goods, services and social network onto the platform, and join a new vision of community, commerce and healthcare that transforms how we heal, grow and collaborate with all that is.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fsection wsection">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="display h-2">Five ways to weave in</h2>
      <p class="wbody">The web holds one person and a whole valley on the same terms. Wherever you&rsquo;re arriving from — yourself, a crew you already run, a community you belong to, the organization you built, or the land you steward — there&rsquo;s a rung that fits, and each one carries the others.</p>
      <WeaveIn />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fsection wsection wsection--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="display h-2">Questions, answered</h2>
      <div class="wfaq">
        <input type="text" id="wfaq-search" class="wfaq-search" placeholder="Search questions" />
        {FAQS.map((f) => (
          <details class="wfaq-item">
            <summary>{f.q}</summary>
            <p>{f.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
        <p class="wfaq-empty" id="wfaq-empty" hidden>No matches — ask below instead.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fsection wsection wstorm" id="weave-with-us">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="wcallout">We&rsquo;re not building a utopia. We&rsquo;re building an ecosystem — where separation is the curriculum, and reconnection is the medicine.</p>
      <span class="eyebrow">Come build it with us</span>
      <h2 class="display h-2">Weave with us</h2>
      <p class="wbody">Every thread in the web is critical to its strength and flexibility. If you&rsquo;re an individual, the door is <a href="/signup" class="wlink">an invitation</a> — every new member receives three months of full Concierge membership, free, and founding members shape the platform as we build it. If you&rsquo;re an organization, community, group or place — a venue, a practice, a piece of land, a body of work — tell us who you are and what you&rsquo;d like to weave in, and a real person will write back to begin the conversation.</p>
      <form class="winquiry" id="winquiry">
        <div class="winquiry-row">
          <input type="text" name="name" placeholder="Your name" required />
          <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="Your email" required />
        </div>
        <textarea name="message" rows="4" placeholder="Who are you, and what would weaving in look like?" required></textarea>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-up">Start the conversation</button>
        <p class="winquiry-status" id="winquiry-status" role="status"></p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>
  </>
)}

{!isAbout && (
  <section class="fsection wsection wstorm" id="weave">
    <div class="container">
      <slot name="weave">
        <span class="eyebrow">The brain/soul-storm</span>
        <h2 class="display h-2">What weaving in could look like</h2>
        <p class="wbody">Every thread in the web is critical to its strength and flexibility in bringing about a better future — an individual joining as an alpha tester to make the platform better, an organization opening a public page and an offering, a community or group bringing its gatherings onto shared infrastructure, a place stewarding land inside the trust. Let&rsquo;s dream it up together.</p>
